      "change": "-1.24% d/d (-92.74 vs May 14 record close 7,501.24); Nasdaq -1.54%; Dow -1.07% (-537); Russell 2000 -2.44% worst day since November; VIX +6.78% to 18.43",
      "tooltip": "S&P 500 7,408.50 (-1.24%); Nasdaq Composite 26,225.14 (-1.54%); Dow Jones 49,526.17 (-1.07%, -537.29 pts); Russell 2000 2,793.30 (-2.44%) — worst day since November, ended 7-week winning streak. May 14 had hit record 7,501.24 intraday/close. Risk-off triggered by: (1) Hormuz tanker seizures (5/14); (2) Trump-Xi summit closed no joint statement; (3) Brent +3.35% / WTI +4.20% oil spike; (4) WSJ/CNBC inflation-and-recession warnings (Niles Investment: '10 of last 12 recessions preceded by oil spike'). 10 of 11 S&P sectors red; energy sole gainer (+1.6%). Tech profit-taking: NVDA -4.4%, INTC -6%, AMD -5.7%, MU -6.6%. Boeing -3.8% on smaller-than-expected China order (200 jets vs expected 500). Bond rout: 10Y UST 4.595% (+14bp, highest in year); 30Y UST 5.121% (+11bp, highest since May 2025)."
    },
